# Dias contributor rule

Before creating or editing lore in this repository:

1. Read [`agent/contributor-start.md`](agent/contributor-start.md).
2. **Always** read and follow the Cursor **story-architect** skill (schema, templates, naming, categories, canon rules). Do not improvise a parallel lore format.
3. Follow [`agent/canon-safety.md`](agent/canon-safety.md) (soft limits, no casual Zero/ferry solves, protect mapped GUID files).
4. Orient with [`agent/world-orientation.md`](agent/world-orientation.md) and [`agent/stage-readiness.md`](agent/stage-readiness.md) before inventing hubs or arcs.
5. Set **`time_era`** and **`time_span`** on every lore entry ([`agent/timeline-metadata.md`](agent/timeline-metadata.md); canon [`world/timeline-metadata-of-dias.md`](world/timeline-metadata-of-dias.md)).

Lore stays in category folders only. Agent ops stay under `agent/`. Keep `GUIDED-PATH.md` steps 1–5 stable.
